# Dex Developer Repository Instructions

This repository is the source of truth for the public Dex Developer skill. Keep
the plugin portable across Codex, Claude Code, and Cursor. Validate every
changed reference against the immutable Dex source in `DEX_BASELINE`.

## Dex AI Platform synchronization

Every pull request must include a paired pull request in
`superdurable/skill-dex-ai-platform`, even when the vendored Core/Go content
does not change. Put this exact field in the Dex Developer pull request body:

```text
Dex-AI-Platform-PR: https://github.com/superdurable/skill-dex-ai-platform/pull/NUMBER
```

In the paired repository, run its `script/sync-dex-developer.py` against the
Dex Developer pull request head with the Dex Developer PR number. Review the
bundled `dex-ai-platform-backend` entrypoint whenever shared or Go guidance
changes; platform-specific rules remain stricter than the generic skill.

Merge pairs serially:

1. finish review and validation in both pull requests;
2. merge the Dex AI Platform pull request first;
3. rerun Dex Developer CI;
4. merge the Dex Developer pull request.

If another Dex Developer change lands first, rebase and regenerate the pair.
Do not bypass, skip, or weaken cross-repository validation. The repositories
are public; synchronization is read-only and must not introduce a cross-repo
write token.

## Release discipline

Skill changes update `VERSION` and `CHANGELOG.md`. A release is valid only
when package/source validation and the Dex AI Platform `main` tree-hash check
all pass. The bundled platform backend is released by Dex AI Platform, not by
this repository.
